RTED\",\"evidence\":\"The gateway refuses a request for three reasons and only one of them is the one above\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states three reasons with only one being the cap described above.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-030\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"A credential may be suspended\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-031\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"a route may be closed for maintenance\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-032\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-033\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"None of those three clears itself by waiting for a stated number of seconds\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states none of the three listed cases clears by waiting.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-034\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-035\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Reading the status code rather than the class it belongs to is what separates the two cases, and it costs one comparison\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states reading the status code costs one comparison.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-036\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"A cap can be raised\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-037\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"the number of caps raised without a measurement behind them is 0\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-038\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Bring a week of refusal counts, the shape of the traffic across the day, and the deadline that traffic is serving\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text lists the same three items to bring.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-039\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"The platform team looks at whether the load is smooth or bursty\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-040\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"a burst is cheaper to smooth than it is to serve at its peak\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-041\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"A caller that can move half its work to a quieter hour usually gets what it needs without any change to the cap at all\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-042\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Requests reach the platform team through the usual channel\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this in the section on asking for an increase.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-043\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"they are answered within two working days\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states the two working day answer time.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-044\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"There is no expedited path and no exception list\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states there is no expedited path.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"A-045\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"There is no expedited path and no exception list\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states there is no exception list.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-001\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Every credential has a cap\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Every credential having a cap carries the same meaning as each having a cap of its own.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-002\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"When that cap is spent the gateway answers 429 at the edge\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-003\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"the gateway answers 429 at the edge — without waking the service behind it\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Not waking the service is the same as not troubling it.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-004\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"An earlier draft of this note argued for a client-side token bucket that mirrored the gateway’s own counters\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-005\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Requests are counted against the credential that presented them, over a fixed window of 60 seconds whose start the gateway doesn’t disclose, and never against a connection\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states counting is by credential and never by connection.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-006\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"over a fixed window of 60 seconds\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states the fixed 60 second window.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-007\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"whose start the gateway doesn’t disclose\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states the window start is not disclosed.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-008\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Opening a second socket therefore buys a caller nothing\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states extra sockets buy the caller nothing.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-009\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"The count follows the credential wherever the caller happens to put it, including across hosts\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-010\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"A client spread across eight worker processes is throttled at exactly the point one process would have been\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states the same point with eight worker processes as the instance of many.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-011\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"The default allowance is 100 requests in a window\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-012\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"The default is enough for every interactive use of this API the platform team has seen\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states the default suffices for every interactive use seen.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-013\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"a caller that needs more than that is almost always doing batch work under an interactive credential\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-014\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"It is the platform declining to spend capacity that has already been promised to somebody else\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text describes the refusal as protecting capacity already promised to somebody else.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-015\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Callers that retry at once are the largest single reason the cap is there at all\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Retrying at once being the largest single reason for the cap conveys the same meaning in different words.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-016\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"The refusal carries a Retry-After header\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text names the header Retry-After.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-017\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Its value is a whole number of seconds to wait\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-018\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"it is present on every refusal the gateway sends\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states the header is on every refusal.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-019\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Waiting that long and then continuing is the whole of the contract\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states waiting and continuing is the whole contract.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-020\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"waiting longer than the header asks earns a caller no credit at all\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states waiting longer earns no credit.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-021\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"The body of the refusal is JSON\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-022\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"it names what the gateway calls the “window” it counted in. It names the cap and the tier as well, all as plain fields\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states the body names the window, cap and tier as plain fields.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-023\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Four rules, given in the order they should be applied\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text gives four rules for how the client retries.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-024\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Four rules, given in the order they should be applied\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states the rules are given in the order of application.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-025\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Honour the header, every time. The gateway has already done that arithmetic, with information the caller does not have, and it does the same on the 503 path, even though the cause of the refusal there is an entirely different one. A wait derived on the client side is a guess about a counter it cannot see\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Rule one is to honour the header, and a client-derived wait is dismissed as a guess.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-026\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"The gateway has already done that arithmetic, with information the caller does not have\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states the gateway computes with information the caller lacks.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-027\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"it does the same on the 503 path\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"Under the honour-the-header rule the text states the gateway does the same on the 503 path, so the rule holds there.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-028\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"even though the cause of the refusal there is an entirely different one\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states the cause on the 503 path is entirely different.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-029\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"Retry only what is safe to retry, which is a smaller set than the set of responses that aren’t a success\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-030\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"A 200 needs nothing\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-031\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"a 429 needs the stated wait\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-032\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"a 500 can be retried once that wait has passed\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-033\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"a 503 means the platform itself is overloaded\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-034\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"The four cases are not interchangeable. A client that folds every non-success into one branch will retry hardest during exactly the incident the cap was installed to survive\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The text says the four cases are not interchangeable and that folding them into one branch retries hardest during the incident.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-035\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"A batch credential is allowed 1000 requests in a window\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this directly.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-036\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"A batch credential is allowed 1000 requests in a window, which is 50 times the default\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states the batch allowance is 50 times the default.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-037\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"not a separate counting scheme\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states the batch allowance is not a separate counting scheme.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-038\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"evidence\":\"The window, the header and the body are identical to the interactive case\",\"evidence_source\":\"merged.md\",\"rationale\":\"The reference text states this under the batch rule.\"},{\"claim_id\":\"B-039\",\"verdict\":\"SUPPOR